KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cerr good: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ cerr precision: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ cerr unitbuf: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ cerr tied to cout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Meaningful only with the MSVC STL (Windows); elsewhere the #error makes it
fail, which is why it is not CORE: the Linux jobs run every CORE test.
provide_standard_stream_objects now defines the stream objects for the MSVC
STL too, and the runtime functions its locale initialization calls are
modelled (_Locinfo_ctor, _Locinfo_dtor, _Getcvt).  With the MSVC 14.51
headers preprocessed by cl (iostream.ii of the VS 2026 CI job) and
--winx64 on Linux, the program verifies in 7 s with these results
(_Getctype and _Mbrtowc, still without a model, are not on its paths).
